From: Iscandar build <iscandar@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0006] iscandar: registry form check at init, not born-empty

First kernel-round boot (2026-11-22, image
elbe-build-20261122-134513): the engine shut at init with
"registry born occupied at 0". The assertion could never
hold: patch 0003 registers caches in every state from the
first cache creation, and kmem_cache_init precedes
postcore_initcall, so the early caches lawfully occupy
the first registry slots before iscandar_init runs. The
Beam mass checks and the ledger born-zero check ahead of
this one passed in the running kernel; the canary never
ran. Replace the born-empty assertion with a form check:
an occupied entry must carry its slot's id (the register
path's staged write, s last); an empty entry must be
wholly zero, as the mass bore it and as the unregister
path leaves it. Ruled by Andrew 2026-11-22 ("go ahead
and make the natural fix"). Desk check: mm/iscandar/
core.o compiles clean against the rebased stack.

---
--- a/mm/iscandar/core.c
+++ b/mm/iscandar/core.c
@@ -576,9 +576,28 @@
 			return 0;
 		}
 	}
+	/* The registry is not born empty, and must not be:
+	 * registration runs in every state from the first
+	 * cache creation (patch 0003), and kmem_cache_init
+	 * precedes this initcall, so the early caches
+	 * lawfully occupy the first slots before init
+	 * runs. What init verifies is form. An occupied
+	 * entry carries the id of its slot (id == slot + 1,
+	 * the register path's staged write, s last); an
+	 * empty entry is wholly zero, as the mass bore it
+	 * and as the unregister path leaves it. Anything
+	 * else is a torn or foreign write: engine shut. */
 	for (i = 0; i < ISCANDAR_REGISTRY_CAP; i++) {
 		if (registry[i].s) {
-			pr_err("iscandar: registry born occupied at %d; engine shut\n",
+			if (registry[i].id != (u32)i + 1) {
+				pr_err("iscandar: registry entry %d malformed: id %u; engine shut\n",
+				       i, registry[i].id);
+				iscandar_state = ISCANDAR_ST_CLOSED;
+				return 0;
+			}
+		} else if (memchr_inv(&registry[i], 0,
+				      sizeof(registry[i]))) {
+			pr_err("iscandar: registry entry %d torn: empty but nonzero; engine shut\n",
 			       i);
 			iscandar_state = ISCANDAR_ST_CLOSED;
 			return 0;
